From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:02:20 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] server: Ignores activation requests without user input.

Any xdg-activation token was accepted, so an application presenting its
window on its own (eg. when a message arrives, together with its
notification) took the keyboard from the window in use, mid-word, and
closed its open menu. Only tokens with a seat are accepted now: wlroots
checked at commit that the serial was given to the client and that the
requesting surface had the focus (a click on a notification's action, on
a launcher). Other requests are logged and ignored.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/server.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/server.c b/src/server.c
index 996bcda..e3793e1 100644
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -1104,7 +1104,13 @@ void handle_request_set_primary_selection(
 /**
  * Handles `request_activate` of `wlr_xdg_activation_v1`: Activates & raises.
  *
- * Any valid token is accepted, ie. there is no focus stealing prevention.
+ * Only a token that stems from user input is accepted: wlroots then checked
+ * that the serial of the seat was given to the client, and that the surface
+ * asking for the token had the focus (eg. the click on a notification's
+ * action, or on a launcher). A token without a seat is an application
+ * presenting itself on its own (a message arrived): That would take the
+ * keyboard from the window in use, mid-word, and close its open menu. Such a
+ * request is ignored; the window stays where it is.
  * Windows that are not on the current workspace are left untouched.
  *
  * @param listener_ptr
@@ -1126,6 +1132,12 @@ void _wlmaker_server_handle_xdg_activation_request_activate(
         event_ptr->surface);
     if (NULL == window_ptr) return;
 
+    if (NULL == event_ptr->token || NULL == event_ptr->token->seat) {
+        bs_log(BS_INFO, "Activation request for window %p without user "
+               "input, ignored (focus stealing prevention).", window_ptr);
+        return;
+    }
+
     wlmtk_workspace_t *workspace_ptr = wlmtk_window_get_workspace(window_ptr);
     if (NULL == workspace_ptr) return;
     if (workspace_ptr != wlmtk_desktop_get_current_workspace(
